cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ballast: agent skills that encode when not to do something"
message: "If you use these skills or build on them, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Jawahar Naidu"
    family-names: "Nettem"
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jawahars07/ballast"
url: "https://github.com/Jawahars07/ballast"
abstract: >-
  Eleven self-authored agent skills for Claude Code and any tool implementing the
  Agent Skills open standard. Where most skills add a capability, these add a
  check: separating what a job description requires from what it merely describes,
  removing the lexical and structural markers of machine-written text, vetting
  third-party code before installation, sweeping a repository before it goes
  public, and enforcing a verification phase in long-running builds. Distributed
  as pure markdown with no executable surface, so the whole corpus can be audited
  by reading it.
keywords:
  - agent-skills
  - claude-code
  - ai-agents
  - prompt-engineering
  - resume
  - applicant-tracking-system
  - supply-chain-security
